Package: os7-base
Version: @OS7_VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Bastian Wirth <bastian.wirth@upinblue.com>
Section: metapackages
Priority: important
Depends: os7-release (= @OS7_VERSION@),
 os7-console (= @OS7_VERSION@),
 os7-powershell (= @OS7_VERSION@),
 os7-module (= @OS7_VERSION@)
Homepage: https://github.com/upinblue/os7
Description: OS/7 — the parts every OS/7 machine has
 A metapackage, and the reason it exists is that membership has to be
 executable rather than descriptive. Before it, "what is an OS/7 system" was a
 sentence in a document and a set of package lists consulted once at image build
 time; nothing on a running machine could answer it, and nothing could converge
 a machine that had drifted.
 .
 THE VERSIONS ARE EXACT. Depending on "= this version" rather than ">=" is what
 makes an update a single apt operation that moves the whole product together:
 installing os7-base at a version pulls every OS/7 component to that same
 version, and a component that failed to build simply makes the transaction
 unsatisfiable instead of shipping a half-moved machine.
 .
 It carries no files. A metapackage with files is a package doing two jobs, and
 the second one cannot be removed without the first.
